## What was measured before it was specified

Nothing in this brief is recalled. The retained script is
`~/.bisellium-evidence/W-130-spec/measure-replay-acceptance.mjs`, read-only,
with its captured transcripts in `cases/` and its output in
`measurement.txt`. It classifies thirteen real transcripts with the predicate
`scripts/run-builder-host.mjs:784-790` uses today and with the one this brief
specifies, and reports **0 disagreements** with the wanted verdict:

- W-110's eight recorded reds: `02` and `03` flip from refused to accepted;
  `01`, `04`, `05`, `06`, `07`, `08` keep today's verdict byte for byte. That
  is the exact scope the dispatch required and it is demonstrated, not claimed.
- Five negatives from a real `@playwright/test` 1.63.0: a passing run, a
  missing browser, a module-load error, an empty selection and a three-failure
  run are each refused, with a distinct reason.

Three measurements corrected the premises the brief was dispatched with, and
the brief records all three:

1. **The missing-browser error carries no `ENOENT`.** Measured text:
   `Error: browserType.launch: Executable doesn't exist at …`, with a
   `  1 failed` summary. Today's poison regex does **not** reject it. So the
   hazard is the opposite of the one assumed: widening acceptance on the
   summary line alone would have let a browserless cell pass a missing browser
   off as a genuine red. The specified predicate therefore requires both
   exactly one failed test and an `expect(…)` matcher banner, and adds
   `browserType.launch` and `Executable doesn't exist` to the poison list so
   the refusal is named rather than incidental.
2. **The gate cell has no gap to close.** `CI_STEPS` is six entries with no
   playwright and no build; `test:suite` registers no playwright; the
   `web-e2e` workflow job is deliberately not a CI step; W-110 is
   `kind: "opus"`, so `effectiveProbationes` adds no `served-e2e` for it, and
   no record anywhere is `kind: ui`. Scoped **out**, stated as a decision with
   its measurement, and filed as a follow-on that becomes live the day a
   record is `kind: ui`.
3. **A fourth defect blocks W-110's reds 2 and 3 independently.**
   `packages/commands/src/lifecycle.ts:877` records `cmd.join(" ")` and the
   replay splits on whitespace, so the quoted `--grep "W-110 behaviour 2: "`
   arrives as five argv words; measured on `layout.spec.ts`, that broadens a
   selection. The information is already lost in the recorded log, so no
   host-side change recovers it. Scoped out with the root cause named, a
   follow-on filed for quote-safe recording, and the zero-code remedy measured
   for W-110: record with a whitespace-free `--grep behaviour.2:`, which
   selects exactly the one test. The predicate's "exactly one failed test"
   clause refuses a broadened replay, so this is enforced rather than trusted.

The design itself was proved in a real cell, not inferred: `bwrap
--unshare-all` with a **read-only** browsers path launched chromium and ran
three specs, and loopback bound and round-tripped in the same cell. A
read-only bind is sufficient; playwright writes nothing into the cache.
`npm --workspace @bisellium/web run build` was timed at 0.66s wall, which is
why the build needs no per-red classifier to be affordable, and `npm` was
confirmed reachable on the replay cell's own PATH.

## The W-125 trust boundary

The brief reconciles explicitly, in its own section, because D-035 obliges the
censor to judge this as a trust-boundary change. In short: W-125's "fixed host
commands, not candidate package scripts selected at runtime" governs the
producer **gate** cell, whose point is that a candidate cannot replace the
host's required suite — and that cell is untouched, still running pinned
`master` tooling from a separate read-only checkout. The **replay** cell has
always executed a candidate-authored command verbatim out of the red log under
confinement, so building there adds no capability: same `sandboxArgs`
descriptor (hoisted to one object so the two cannot drift), same private
`HOME`/`/tmp`, same `--unshare-all`, same read-only system tree, no host repo,
no credentials, and the host reads nothing out of the build but an exit status
and output text the candidate could already shape.

The stricter shape is imposed anyway where it is free: one hardcoded host
argv, gated on a fixed host path so no candidate selection occurs; a
preparation failure that is a distinct message prefix and a hard run failure,
never an accepted red; a required `apps/web/dist/index.html` so a build that
exits 0 without a bundle is caught; and behaviour 3(e) proving from inside the
cell that the build saw no credential, no host file and no egress. The browser
bind grants read and nothing else — behaviours 1 and 2 assert `EROFS` from
inside both cells, and the cache is `npx playwright install` output with no
secret in it. One residual is stated rather than hidden: playwright launches
chromium with `--no-sandbox`, so bwrap's namespaces are the only boundary
around it — W-125's already-accepted trusted computing base with a larger
third-party binary inside it.

## Scope

Three named changes, five behaviours, five files, one existing assertion edited
(`run.test.ts:670`, `18` → `19`, forced by the one new environment name and
named in the behaviour that forces it). The one addition beyond the three
changes is `scripts/replay-accept.mjs`: a pure classifier extracted so its
table of near-miss transcripts is a millisecond test instead of five full
confined runs, with the wiring pinned separately so the mechanism cannot go
untested (L-040). Two latent defects found on the `kind: ui` path — a regex
that cannot match the quoted kind every record writes, and a probe hunting a
system `chromium` the tool PATH does not carry — are left alone with their
reason: fixing the regex alone would make every ui builder fail its probe.
Both are in the second follow-on filing.

No new dependency, verb, flag, wire attribute, lifecycle id, receipt field or
doc edit is authorized. `docs/ADOPTION.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` are a
measured deliberate non-change: neither documents the cells' binds or
environment allowlist, and no package edge, seam, lifecycle transition or
serve route moves.

Signed as ready for a builder. No implementation, evidence or review verdict is
claimed by this signature; D-014's censor supplies the single independent
implementation review.
